1. Pick up the attendance register from the faculty desk.
2. Place the projector remote on the classroom podium.
3. Open the library storage cabinet.
4. Close the classroom door.
5. Move the notice board stand near the administrative office.
6. Pick up the laboratory safety goggles from the equipment shelf.
7. Place the visitor register on the reception desk.
8. Turn off the classroom projector.
9. Pick up the attendance register and place it on the faculty desk.
10. Open the library cabinet and retrieve the requested book.
11. Pick up the laboratory notebook and place it on the experiment table.
12. Retrieve the seminar microphone and place it on the auditorium podium.
13. Open the stationery cabinet and collect a box of markers.
14. Pick up the classroom keys and place them at the reception desk.
15. Retrieve the student assignment box and place it in the faculty office.
16. Pick up the recycling bin and place it beside the classroom entrance.
17. Go to the library, retrieve the requested book, and deliver it to the reading room.
18. Navigate to Classroom 101, collect the projector remote, and return it to the faculty office.
19. Go to the laboratory, retrieve the microscope, and place it on the preparation table.
20. Navigate to the administrative office, collect the visitor register, and place it at the reception desk.
21. Go to the seminar hall, retrieve the microphone, and place it on the auditorium podium.
22. Navigate to the faculty office, collect the attendance register, and deliver it to Classroom 202.
23. Go to the equipment room, retrieve the extension cable, and place it in the seminar hall.
24. Navigate to the cafeteria, collect the meal tray, and return it to the tray collection area.
25. If the requested book is available in the library, deliver it to the reading room; otherwise notify the librarian by placing the request form on the desk.
26. If the classroom door is open after lectures, close it before leaving the building.
27. If the projector remote is missing from the classroom podium, retrieve one from the equipment room.
28. If the laboratory safety goggles are unavailable in the laboratory, bring a set from the storage cabinet.
29. If the visitor register is already at the reception desk, organize the information counter; otherwise place the register on the desk.
30. If the seminar hall is occupied, place the microphone on the preparation table; otherwise place it on the podium.
31. If the stationery cabinet is open, close it before leaving the administrative office.
32. Carry the microscope without tilting or dropping it.
33. Transport the projector carefully without disconnecting its cables.
34. Carry the stack of books without allowing any to fall.
35. Move the laboratory glassware box carefully without breaking any items.
36. Place the computer monitor on the desk without covering the keyboard.
37. Transport the seminar microphone without placing it on the floor.
38. Move the notice board stand without blocking the corridor.
39. Prepare Classroom 101 by arranging chairs, placing the projector remote on the podium, distributing markers, checking the whiteboard, and returning to the faculty office.
40. Restock the laboratory by collecting safety goggles, laboratory notebooks, measuring instruments, and gloves from storage, placing each item in its designated location, and returning to the equipment room.
41. Inspect the library, classrooms, laboratories, seminar hall, and administrative office for misplaced equipment, open cabinets, and unattended materials, correct each issue, and return to the reception desk.
42. Collect assignment boxes from multiple classrooms, deliver them to the faculty office, organize the office desk, and return to the administrative building entrance.
43. Prepare the seminar hall by arranging chairs, placing the microphone on the podium, organizing presentation materials, checking the projector, and returning to the equipment room.
44. Prepare the college for the next academic session by organizing classrooms, restocking laboratory supplies, arranging library materials, securing administrative documents, and returning to the reception desk.
45. Perform a complete campus facility inspection by checking classrooms, laboratories, the library, seminar hall, administrative office, and reception area for misplaced items, open doors, unattended equipment, or incomplete setup, resolve each issue, and return to the administration office.
